    "summary": "Texas shows widespread resistance: most counties score high, and about 35 moratoria are tallied. The standouts are Hays (5-0 county water pause and a San Marcos ban), Denton, Cameron (Brownsville and Harlingen moratoria), Austin County (a countywide moratorium) and Lubbock, with Archer, Brazoria, Somervell and Caldwell also denying incentives or passing resolutions. Counterweights are that counties lack zoning power, as seen when Hill County rescinded its moratorium after a $100M lawsuit, and that Armstrong, Nolan and Taylor counties lean toward approval, with many high scores resting on thin local evidence."
